OL,3,AVolcano eruption leaves 170,000
OL,4,Apassengers stranded in Indonesia
OL,5,
OL,6,FAround 170,000 passengers have been
OL,7,Fleft stranded after a volcanic eruption
OL,8,Fforced Indonesian authorities to
OL,9,Ftemporarily suspend operations at eight
OL,10,Fairports.
OL,12,FJakarta's Soekarno-Hatta International
OL,13,FAirport was the first to be closed on
OL,14,FSunday morning after ash from Anak
OL,15,FKrakatau was detected in airspace near
OL,16,Fthe airport.
OL,18,FThe transport ministry said 1,558
OL,19,Fflights have been delayed with airports
OL,20,Fremaining closed until midnight.
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,0,100
